course: dictionary
lesson: 5277
title: Judgment in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Judgment is a word with more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one is meant. It can mean good, sensible decisions, an opinion you form after thinking, or a decision made by a court. It is also spelled judgement, and both spellings are correct.
explain: «Use your judgment» in PSHE means think it through before you act, for example before you share something online. Ask yourself what a sensible person would do. «Do not think of yourself more highly than you ought, but rather think of yourself with sober judgment» (Romans 12:3) means think clearly and honestly about yourself.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a word such as "good sense" or "decision". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. In law, «the court gives its judgment» means the judge makes an official decision.
fact: Judgment means the ability to make good, sensible decisions.
fact: A judgment can also be an opinion you form after thinking about something.
fact: In law, a judgment is a decision made by a judge or a court.
fact: «Good judgment» and «use your judgment» mean think it through before you act.
fact: Judgment Day, or the Last Judgment, is when Christians believe God will judge all people at the end of time.
exercise: «Use your judgment before you share a photo online.» What does use your judgment mean here? | Share it with everyone at once | Forget about it straight away | Take another photo | *Think it through before you act
exercise: «The court gave its judgment in the case.» What is a judgment in law? | A rule about school lunches | *A decision made by a judge or a court | A quick guess made by a child | A picture painted on a church wall
exercise: «Do not think of yourself more highly than you ought, but rather think of yourself with sober judgment» (Romans 12:3). What does sober judgment mean? | Wrong and confused | *Clear, honest thinking | Loud and cheerful | Hurried and silly
test: «He went ahead with the plan against his better judgment.» What does against my better judgment mean? | *Even though he thought it was not sensible | By accident and without thinking | In a hurry, before anyone could stop him | With great courage and no fear
test: «In my judgment, the film is good.» In this sentence, judgment means about the same as which word? | ladder | puddle | *opinion | puzzle
exam: «She showed good judgment and waited for help.» Which sentence uses judgment in the same way? | *Her good judgment kept her safe on the icy path | He ate his lunch quickly | The judge read out the judgment in the trial | The bus was late again
